  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contracting in North Carolina totaled $3.9B in obligations for FY2026 to date. Obligations fell down 58.1% year over year. Contract activity included 146,345 awards with an average award size of $26.7K. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.7B, followed by the General Services Administration at $513M and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $503M. GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. is the largest vendor at $176M, followed by SDV OFFICE SYSTEMS LLC at $170M and RESEARCH TRIANGLE INSTITUTE at $168M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest industry by obligations at $330M, with Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $282M and Engineering Services at $254M also significant. FY2026 to date obligations are lower than recent fiscal years that peaked at $9.3B in FY25. These figures cover fiscal year to date obligations and do not represent a full fiscal year total.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are the biggest buyers in North Carolina?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.7B in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $513M and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $503M. Other top buyers include the Department of Health and Human Services at $312M and the Department of Homeland Security at $292M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What industries and vendors dominate federal contracting in North Carolina?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest industry at $330M, followed by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $282M and Engineering Services at $254M. GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. is the largest vendor at $176M, with SDV OFFICE SYSTEMS LLC at $170M and RESEARCH TRIANGLE INSTITUTE at $168M."
      }
    ]
  },
